   124	## Window-credit and DNS formulas
   125	
   126	Let `KiB=1024 B`, bandwidth be integer bits/s, RTT integer ns:
   127	
   128	```text
   129	W32 = 32 × KiB
   130	W64 = 64 × KiB
   131	rawBDPBytes = ceil(bandwidthBitsPerSecond × rttNanoseconds /
   132	                   (8 × 1_000_000_000))
   133	cappedBDP = clamp(rawBDPBytes, bulkWindowMinimumBytes,
   134	                  bulkWindowMaximumBytes)
   135	relayBurstBytes = relayBurstDatagramCount ×
   136	                  max(4 + relayMaximumFrameBodyBytes, 64)
   137	relayCandidate = min(relayWindowMaximumBytes,
   138	                     relayControlWindowBytes + relayBurstBytes)
   139	```
   140	
   141	For requested `W`:
   142	
   143	```text
   144	channelCharge = W + readBufferReservation + writeReservation + metadata
   145	
   146	admit iff W <= perChannelWindowCeiling
   147	  and laneWindowReserved + W <= perLaneWindowCeiling
   148	  and globalWindowReserved + W <= globalWindowCeiling
   149	  and ledgerCommittedBytes + channelCharge <= globalLedgerCeilingBytes
   150	  and lane is current, healthy, not closing, and not in KEX
   151	  and pressure policy permits the class
   152	```
   153	
   154	Initial credit is at most the reserved immutable cap. `WINDOW_ADJUST(delta)`
   155	requires an atomic reservation while the generation is current and state is
   156	Normal or Soft. Pressure, Critical, KEX, closing, failed, stale, or insufficient
   157	budget withholds it. Previously advertised credit is never revoked/reclaimed.
   158	No failed adjustment is queued on the side.
   159	
   160	```text
   161	delta = min(channelCap - outstandingAdvertisedCredit,
   162	            laneWindowHeadroom, globalWindowHeadroom,
   163	            ledgerHeadroomAfterOtherReservations)
   164	```
   165	
   166	`delta=0` is withholding. Until M3 delivers consumer-earned immutable credit,
   167	libssh2 wire metrics stay `unsupported/notReported`; bounded adapter intake and
   168	the conservative reservation remain mandatory.
   169	
   170	For endpoints `E`, owners `O`, maximum DNS message `M`, queued wire `Q`:
   171	
   172	```text
   173	framedMessage = M + 2
   174	perOwner = 3 × framedMessage + 1,024
   175	fixed = 2 × framedMessage + 65,536 manager + 65,536 diagnostics + 64 × E + Q
   176	dnsLocalLedger = O × perOwner + fixed
   177	dnsSlack = dnsAggregateBytes - dnsLocalLedger
   178	```
   179	
   180	```text
   181	default: E=4, O=16, M=65,535, Q=262,144
   182	         3,686,706 <= 4,194,304; slack 507,598
   183	hard:    E=8, O=32, M=65,535, Q=1,048,576
   184	         7,635,554 <= 8,388,608; slack 753,054
   185	```
   186	
   187	Equality is accepted; one byte over any component/aggregate is typed refusal.
   188	The manager reserves the complete component before capability publication.
   189	Unused DNS slack stays DNS-owned until an atomic transfer, preventing two owners
   190	from spending the same residual byte.
   191	
   192	## Pressure states and hysteresis
   193	
   194	Configuration supplies three entry headroom floors and three higher exit floors
   195	for ledger, physical-footprint, and advisory signals:
   196	
   197	```text
   198	criticalEnter < pressureEnter < softEnter
   199	criticalExit > criticalEnter
   200	pressureExit > pressureEnter
   201	softExit > softEnter
   202	```
   203	
   204	Each observation records generation/time, footprint/peak, ledger
   205	current/reserved/committed/peak, one new advisory-call result, warning input,
   206	and owner report states. Severity is the maximum entry predicate across ledger
   207	headroom, configured footprint headroom, fresh advisory bytes, and explicit
   208	memory warning (at least Pressure). Entry may jump severity.
   209	
   210	Exit moves at most one state/evaluation and requires every available signal
   211	above the exit floor, required actions acknowledged, no unresolved owner-read
   212	failure, and a configured recovery dwell. This is hysteresis, not averaging.
   213	An advisory value is fresh only in the observation that called the API.
   214	Unavailable, failed, malformed, or late results are typed; they cannot cause
   215	recovery, become zero, or conceal escalation from other evidence. In Normal
   216	they do not alone stop the provider; hard ledger fit still governs admission.
   217	
   218	## One ordered action table
   219	
   220	The serialized executor applies rows cumulatively and keys each action by
   221	`(policyGeneration, ordinal, owner)`.
   222	
   223	| # | State | Action | Completion/failure semantics |
   224	| ---: | --- | --- | --- |
   225	| 1 | Soft | Suppress optional-lane admission | Lane A remains; optional request fast-refuses `memoryPressure` |
   226	| 2 | Soft | Close contract-defined idle channels/associations | No live-stream migration or arbitrary kill; timeout blocks recovery |
   227	| 3 | Soft | Cap new channel windows at configured soft value | Existing advertised credit unchanged |
   228	| 4 | Soft | Shrink semantics-safe DNS/relay/packet/other caches and queues | Ack released bytes; no unsafe eviction |
   229	| 5 | Pressure | Withhold all new `WINDOW_ADJUST` | No pending-adjust side queue |
   230	| 6 | Pressure | Reduce HEV session admission and reversible HEV/cache limits | Existing sessions remain accounted; refusal is bounded/typed |
   231	| 7 | Pressure | Fast-refuse new nonessential TCP/UDP/bulk/optional control work | Mandatory safe DNS/control uses its reserved slice; no physical fallback |
   232	| 8 | Critical | Freeze/cancel a replacement not yet started | Bytes stay reserved until actual cleanup ack |
   233	| 9 | Critical | Release old transport, channels, DNS/relay generation, timers, callbacks | Must observe release before replacement construction; no replay/migration |
   234	| 10 | Critical | If continuity is requested, reserve critical bootstrap then start replacement | New lane A includes KEX/DNS/relay mandatory slices |
   235	| 11 | Critical | If release/replacement cannot fit or finish by deadline, stop explicitly | `memoryRecoveryImpossible`; cancel retries, withdraw capability/settings, await bounded cleanup; never jetsam |
   236	
   237	Acknowledgements record requested/released/remaining bytes, owner generation,
   238	deadline outcome, and failure. Duplicate/stale acknowledgements are counted and
   239	ignored. Soft/Pressure failure holds state and refuses dependent admission.
   240	Critical failure proceeds to explicit stop. Recovery reverses only admission
   241	and cache targets; it never recreates closed owners or returns prior credit.
   242	
   243	## Rekey, reconnect, cancellation, and stop
   244	
   245	Each lane permanently reserves `perLaneKEXEmergencyBytes`, allowing inbound
   246	server KEX or a due client security threshold under pressure. Before KEX, the
   247	lane becomes unavailable for new channels. Existing channels remain pinned and
   248	inside existing reservations. One KEX runs/lane; simultaneous triggers coalesce
   249	into it with at most one bounded later-due reason bitset.
   250	
   251	Pressure uses the emergency slice for protocol-required server or due client
   252	KEX while withholding new channels/credit; manual/test triggers defer in the
   253	bounded bitset. Critical lets an active KEX finish only for the retained lane
   254	inside reservation, otherwise closes it during old release/stop. Success
   255	releases old keys/scratch and resumes admission only when current state permits.
   256	Failure is lane-fatal first, closes its channels once, updates lane-A relay/DNS
   257	capability before publication, and requests only an admitted replacement. No
   258	bytes are replayed or migrated.
   259	
   260	```text
   261	replacementBootstrapReservation =
   262	  newTransportBase + mandatoryLaneA + laneAKEXEmergency +
   263	  mandatoryDNSBootstrap + mandatoryRelayBootstrap + lifecycleOverhead
   264	
   265	admit iff oldTransportCharge + replacementBootstrapReservation
   266	           <= reconnectOverlapBytesCeiling
   267	       and ledgerCommittedBytes + replacementBootstrapReservation
   268	           <= globalLedgerCeilingBytes
   269	```
   270	
   271	At Critical the old charge must reach zero before the replacement constructor.
   272	Stop/cancel invalidates generations, cancels admissions/retries, and waits for
   273	actual cleanup before release. Late callbacks cannot allocate, publish
   274	capability, adjust credit, restart timers, or release current-generation bytes.
   275	
   276	Normative views:
   277	[`memory pressure`](../diagrams/TASK-260715-1pn983_memory-pressure-state.puml)
   278	and [`reconnect/rekey`](../diagrams/TASK-260715-1pn983_reconnect-rekey-state.puml).
   279	
   280	## Metrics, evidence, and privacy
   281	
   282	Every metric has a fixed unit, bounded labels, owner, availability state,
   283	monotonic time, generation, and current/peak meaning. Required families cover:
   284	
   285	- footprint/peak and fresh advisory bytes;
   286	- ledger current/reserved/committed/headroom/peak by fixed consumer;
   287	- packet buffers/queues/drops and HEV tasks/sessions/buffers/caches/queues;
   288	- lanes/channels/window cap/reservation/wire-credit report, adjustments,
   289	  read buffers, pending writes/operations;
   290	- DNS owners/buffers/cache/queue/aggregate/slack/refusals;
   291	- client relay associations/frame/queue/control reservations and drops;
   292	- KEX reservation/triggers/active generation/duration/result;
   293	- reconnect old/new reservation, overlap peak, release order, denial/stop;
   294	- action request/ack/timeout/failure/released bytes and transitions;
   295	- tasks/timers/sockets/descriptors and cleanup reconciliation.
   296	
   297	Labels are fixed enums: consumer, lane role, channel class, pressure state,
   298	action ordinal, availability, typed reason. Never capture payload, DNS name,
   299	destination, full address, username, host, fingerprint, credential reference,
   300	command/stdin, path, or stable device ID. Restricted packet/Instruments evidence
   301	follows the M3 custody protocol and is never a board attachment. Unavailable is
   302	never pass.
   303	
   304	## Required invariant and negative tests
   305	
   306	Tests drive production entry points, not helpers preloaded with valid inputs.
   307	Each gate is proved by narrowing a bound or bypassing one lifecycle branch.
   308	
   309	| Invariant | Negative proof | Production boundary / owner |
   310	| --- | --- | --- |
   311	| Global reservation | One-byte-smaller global/component ceiling under concurrent admission refuses exactly one owner | ledger entry used by channel/DNS/relay/lane/reconnect; pressure/fault tasks |
   312	| DNS equality/one-over | `7,635,554` fits `8,388,608`; add one to any term or shrink aggregate by one and publication fails | DNS composition; DNS/fault owners |
   313	| Credit not allocation/reclaim | Stall consumer and spend prior credit; no eager-allocation claim, false reclaim, or Pressure adjustment passes | real adapter open/read path; window/M3 owners |
   314	| No side queue | Narrow queue bytes/count under flood; bounded refusal/drop and no second queue | actual channel/packet/relay enqueue; fault owner |
   315	| State/hysteresis | Equality and one-under/over for every edge; stale/unavailable cannot recover | provider observation; sampler owner |
   316	| Fresh advisory call | Second read fails after high first value; production observation reports failure, not reuse | platform sampler; sampler owner |
   317	| Ordered actions | Fail/timeout each ordinal; later success cannot launder missing release | pressure executor; pressure owner |
   318	| Reconnect overlap | Narrow replacement by one on normal/retry/resume/recovery/critical paths; all refuse or release old first | replacement constructor; pressure owner |
   319	| KEX serialization | Race all triggers/channel open/Pressure/close/stop; one current KEX, no new channel | per-lane trigger/event entry; coordinator |
   320	| Rekey isolation | Inject each adapter failure; affected lane first, close once, no replay/migration | lane KEX completion; isolation owner |
   321	| Forged/stale evidence | Correctly shaped stale reservation/action/KEX/reconnect ack cannot release/publish current state | serialized owners; fault task |
   322	| Cancel/stop cleanup | Cancel every seam and deliver late callbacks; all ownership returns baseline | provider stop/component teardown; fault task |
   323	| Privacy | Prohibited sentinels at every source appear nowhere in composed export | diagnostics export, not formatter helper; instrumentation |
   324	
   325	## M0–M3 ownership and interface map
   326	
   327	| Surface | Required contract | Owner |
   328	| --- | --- | --- |
   329	| M0 packet/HEV | effective socket read-back, accepted 500/24,576/4,096/2 baseline, bounded queues, unavailable internal gauges, cleanup | accepted `TASK-260715-2jatnd`; pressure integration |
