    96	## Memory budget
    97	
    98	The provisional steady-state target for the full extension is 25–30 MiB on the
    99	baseline physical iPhone. This is an engineering target, not an Apple contract.
   100	The provider samples `os_proc_available_memory()` as advisory data and does not
   101	cache it.
   102	
   103	Pressure behavior is ordered:
   104	
   105	1. Soft watermark: stop opening optional lanes, close idle channels, cap new
   106	   channel windows, and shrink caches.
   107	2. Pressure watermark: withhold SSH window adjustments, reduce HEV session/cache
   108	   limits, and refuse new nonessential flows with fast errors.
   109	3. Critical watermark: release the old transport before a controlled reconnect;
   110	   if recovery is impossible, stop with an explicit error rather than relying on
   111	   jetsam.
   112	
   113	SSH advertised window credit is not assumed to be eagerly allocated memory, but
   114	buffering permitted by windows is included in the worst-case budget. Channel
   115	counts, HEV sessions, socket buffers, DNS cache, relay buffers, and reconnect
   116	overlap MUST appear in memory tests.
   117	
