 ## 2026-08-30
 
+### Cross-layer memory authority separates reservation from physical evidence (TASK-260715-1pn983)
+
+- DECISION: One checked-byte ledger owns packet, HEV, SSH, DNS, client relay, rekey, metrics, and reconnect admissions. SSH credit is separate from resident bytes but reserves permitted local storage; failed reads are unknown, never zero or absence.
+- DNS RESIDUAL: The hard candidate ledger is 7,635,554 bytes inside an 8,388,608-byte component budget. Combined with the accepted 9,715,712-byte incremental HEV/bridge peak, it leaves 8,110,080 bytes in the lower 25 MiB engineering envelope. This proves arithmetic fit only; production remains false pending complete physical composition.
+- PRESSURE: Deterministic Soft/Pressure/Critical entry, hysteretic one-level recovery, one ordered action table, KEX emergency reservation, atomic replacement reservation, old-transport-first Critical release, and explicit stop replace jetsam-driven or side-queue behavior.
+- GAPS: Final watermarks, BDP/window winners, component ceilings, untracked reserve, overlap, and iPhone rows remain evidence-gated. No Apple guarantee, payload capture, flow migration, or weakened gate is asserted.
+
 ### M0 packet bridge and HEV baseline accepted (TASK-260715-2jatnd)
 
 - DECISION: The macOS-first M0 Bridge gate passes under ADR-024 with MTU 1500, requested/effective 32768-byte socket buffers, 64-packet/5-ms pump budgets, HEV task-stack/TCP/UDP-copy values 24576/4096/2, and an initial measured 500-session ceiling. MTU 4096 remains injectable behind end-to-end proof; MTU 8500 is a named failed default candidate because constrained-buffer rows produced 768 `EMSGSIZE` refusals.
 - EVIDENCE: Public-API bridge, IPv4/IPv6 framing, deterministic faults, hostile-frame fuzzing, bounded pressure, lifecycle, packaging, notices, and physical Mac MTU/memory rows trace to accepted task-scoped resources in `docs/TASK-260715-2jatnd_m0-bridge-hev-decision-adr.md`. The worst measured incremental HEV/bridge cost was 9,715,712 bytes at 500 sessions; whole-extension SSH/DNS/relay/cache/reconnect memory remains unmeasured.
 - FORK: Unmodified HEV `ad7600497931205105b08367bd1b450048157e40` remains selected. There is no Instruments material-bottleneck evidence or improved callback prototype, so fork authorization is rejected by default.
 - GAPS: Physical iPhone, jetsam, NAT64, sleep/wake, energy, and whole-extension memory stay deferred/blocked and are never inferred from macOS. M1 consumers may use this baseline only through the exact accepted-outcome binding task; production composition remains fail-closed on its other M0 inputs.
 
 ## 2026-08-27
 
 ### 0824 — Deterministic lifecycle release is separated from Darwin residency (TASK-260715-135rr8)
 - ROOT CAUSE: The rev3 gate coupled two distinct claims. Harness-owned channels, reads, queues, boundary/native lifecycle counters, and descriptor-close stages were released deterministically, but the gate still required Darwin to return allocator pages during the same 500-cycle observation. One reviewer run therefore failed on a bounded `+180224 B` non-decreasing footprint rise while the next two passed.
 - FIX: The schema-2 lifecycle evidence now records an `ownedResourcesReleased` verdict and every underlying ownership field for each cycle. The production gate requires 500 cycles, zero failed owned-resource-release cycles, and the unchanged post-warmup maximum resident-footprint drawup ceiling of `256 KiB`. Monotonic and late rises remain classified with exact transition/cycle evidence, but OS page-return timing is no longer used as a proxy for product-owned release. The matrix atomically emits its exact-tree-bound raw report before returning a failing verdict.
